# Website Redirection Vulnerability Explanation

Website redirection vulnerabilities can occur when:
1. A website accepts user input without proper validation
2. The input is used to construct URLs or navigation
3. An attacker can inject malicious URLs

## Common Vulnerabilities:
- Open Redirects (when a site trusts user-supplied URLs)
- Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) that can modify page content
- Server-side vulnerabilities that allow URL manipulation

## Example of a Vulnerable Redirect (for educational purposes):

```php
<?php
// This is an example of vulnerable code - DO NOT USE IN PRODUCTION
if (isset($_GET['redirect'])) {
    $url = $_GET['redirect'];
    header("Location: $url");
    exit();
}
?>
```

